From f784c00e34b2c858472ab8d315b44014fcc37f18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomtomnet <tompere8000@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 08:45:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] ui/sdl2: own Wayland swapchain for the guest's frames,
 partial copies, stats

- the guest's scanout is copied into dmabuf buffers of QEMU's own
  (linux-dmabuf feedback, scanout tranche) and attached to the window's surface,
  so the host compositor scans it out directly; no Mesa swapchain churn
- QEMU_SDL_PARTIAL_COPY=1 (opt-in): copy only the guest's damage since each
  buffer's last fill; QEMU_SDL_COPY_VERIFY=N checks it against full copies
- frame and input statistics, presentation feedback for the vblank regulator

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8iTzFPtyk2Gzbt6CLnRYK
